<h2>What was left out</h2>
<p>A launch price is not in the table even when the lab printed one. The <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> on this site is to label a vendor figure as the vendor’s, and prices on these pages have already been revised inside a single product family. A score on someone else’s index is left out for the same reason. Where a story on this site reports one, the link in the last column goes to that story and to the lab post it cites.</p>
<p>The table is also not a census. It stops at releases whose primary page was open on 21 November 2026 and whose maker, date, and announcement could be tied to that page. Genie 4, NVIDIA’s Nemotron Transcribe, Pika H3 Flex, MiniMax H3-Image, and Microsoft’s MAI weights plan are covered as stories and are not rows here. The next edit should add a row only when a new lab page has been read, and it should change a cell only when that page has changed. The date at the top of this page moves when that happens, not when the site is rebuilt.</p>
